,"shared_category_count":4},{"business_id":"kdqoDMuvyNedsouc1i33vQ","name":"Araña Taqueria y Cantina","shared_categories":"Food, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"mhrW9O0O5hXGXGnEYBVoag","name":"Jacques-Imo's Cafe","shared_categories":"Restaurants, Seafood","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"8KnMSrMuTI2AtHZ2LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"Restaurants, Seafood","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"TMBbCDQG6bENJoQSST0XiA","name":"Brigtsen's Restaurant","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"_C7QiQQc47AOEv4PE3Kong","name":"Commander's Palace","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"Food","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"TcNZXteosegb1RO4O5hREw","review_id":"QL-sbzlGzY5Kq3e-JNvscA","date":"2012-06-17T13:19:22","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9621894955635071,"text_excerpt":"We found this place on Yelp and were in the mood for a po boy so we decided to check it out. This place is out of the Quarter but we enjoyed taking the trolley and seeing some real New Orleans out of the Quarter. I got the roast beef po boy and it was good, but I had to add salt, pepper, and hot sauce to give the meat flavor. I did like all the gravy though. The wife tried the surf and turf and it was the best po boy she ever had. I had a bite and I think I agree. Next time, it will be surf and turf for me. It's a combo of fried shrimp and roast beef with gravy. We also tried the sweet potato fries and they were excellent. With so many places that serve po boys there is some stiff competi..."},{"business_id":"TcNZXteosegb1RO4O5hREw","review_id":"3GpT2PiVWJU6iu_SsNNsew","date":"2014-09-09T02:37:06","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9554943442344666,"text_excerpt":"I love Parkway. I find a hard time choosing between a roast beef (special request to make it extra sloppy) or a fried shrimp poboy. Both are excellent and the epitome of what a good New Orleans Poboy should be. The bread is good fresh POBOY bread. The roast beef is one of the best in the city. It has the right flavor and its super tender and almost melts in your mouth. The shrimp is a close second for me. I like how they pile it up high so they are falling off the bread. The fries and onion rings are good too. Polish it off with a Barqs root beer and you have yourself the perfect New Orleans lunch."},{"business_id":"TcNZXteosegb1RO4O5hREw","review_id":"Q0Igq6sK4j-auFwRL8ZTXw","date":"2012-10-02T20:05:32","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9552022814750671,"text_excerpt":"I was in New Orleans for a few nights, and got the recommendation to try Parkway Bakery and Tavern from a local. The restaurant had a good line-up of people, which to a visitor is always a good sign, because if lot's of people are willing to wait for this food it's bound to be good. It also appeared to be filled with mostly locals, which is also a positive sign. Eating at local establishments usually yields a better food experience than eating at the touristy joints. I looked over the menu, and talked to a man on staff who explained the whole ordering process to me and made some recommendations. I got the large surf 'n turf po'boy, roast beef and shrimp. The po'boy was huge, filling and d..."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"TcNZXteosegb1RO4O5hREw","photo_id":"IuD-lqb616rKkKvBHlPdYQ","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/IuD-lqb616rKkKvBHlPdYQ.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8351259827613831},{"business_id":"TcNZXteosegb1RO4O5hREw","photo_id":"TRrNofpTavfB